  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. For a positive integer MMM, sequence BBB is defined as B=A∗MB = A*MB=A∗M that is, appending AAA exactly MMM times. For example, If A=[1,2]A = [1, 2]A=[1,2] and M=3M = 3M=3, then B=A∗M=[1,2,1,2,1,2]B = A*M = [1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2]B=A∗M=[1,2,1,2,1,2]\n\nYou have to help him to find out the minimum value of MMM such that the length of the **longest strictly increasing subsequence** is maximum possible.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n###Output:\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the **minimum** value of MMM.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤5001 \\le T \\le 5001≤T≤500\n1≤N≤2∗1051 \\le N \\le 2*10^51≤N≤2∗105\n1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109\nIt's guaranteed that the total length of the sequence AAA in one test file doesn't exceed 2∗1062*10^62∗106",
    "constraints": [],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n2 1\n2\n1 2\n5\n1 3 2 1 2",
        "output": "2\n1\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn the first test case, Choosing M=2M = 2M=2 gives B=[2,1,2,1]B = [2, 1, 2, 1]B=[2,1,2,1] which has a longest strictly increasing sequence of length 222 which is the maximum possible.\nIn the second test case, Choosing M=1M = 1M=1 gives B=[1,2]B  = [1, 2]B=[1,2] which has a longest strictly increasing sequence of length 222 which is the maximum possible."
      }
    ]
